1
00:02:30,084 --> 00:02:35,084
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,084 --> 00:02:39,084
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:39,084 --> 00:02:43,084
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:43,084 --> 00:02:48,084
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:48,084 --> 00:02:51,084
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:51,084 --> 00:02:54,084
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:54,084 --> 00:02:57,084
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:57,084 --> 00:03:00,084
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:02,084 --> 00:03:04,084
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:04,084 --> 00:03:07,084
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:07,084 --> 00:03:10,084
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:10,084 --> 00:03:15,084
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:27,084 --> 00:03:33,084
I'm so full, I think I'm gonna puff!

14
00:03:33,084 --> 00:03:36,084
I think I just gained ten pounds!

15
00:03:36,084 --> 00:03:38,084
Navy food sure beats bread and water!

16
00:03:38,084 --> 00:03:42,084
Bread? Ha! We were lucky to eat dirt back there!

17
00:03:42,084 --> 00:03:44,084
Good thing our hero came!

18
00:03:44,084 --> 00:03:48,084
Good forever on your deck, Captain Buggy! Thank you!

19
00:03:48,084 --> 00:03:54,084
No problem, lads! You're all very welcome!

20
00:03:54,084 --> 00:03:57,084
So, how much longer before we get there, Jinbei?

21
00:03:57,084 --> 00:03:59,084
What? Hmm?

22
00:03:59,084 --> 00:04:01,084
The what-me, you turd!

23
00:04:01,084 --> 00:04:03,084
When are we gonna arrive at Navy HQ?

24
00:04:03,084 --> 00:04:07,084
I'm ready to throw down and show those damn dirtbags who's boss!

25
00:04:07,084 --> 00:04:09,084
What an inspirational attitude!

26
00:04:09,084 --> 00:04:11,084
I know, I can't stop shaking!

27
00:04:11,084 --> 00:04:14,084
The seven warlords who sold their souls to the world government

28
00:04:14,084 --> 00:04:16,084
and those three admirals!

29
00:04:16,084 --> 00:04:19,084
They're no match for the likes of us, are they men?

30
00:04:19,084 --> 00:04:20,084
That's right!

31
00:04:20,084 --> 00:04:22,084
You should be the next king of the pirates, Captain Buggy!

32
00:04:22,084 --> 00:04:25,084
Cause you're doing just what Gold Roger would do!

33
00:04:28,084 --> 00:04:31,084
A special retrospective before Marineford!

34
00:04:31,084 --> 00:04:34,084
The three Navy Admirals come together!

35
00:04:35,084 --> 00:04:38,084
Meanwhile, at Navy Headquarters in Marineford...

36
00:04:41,084 --> 00:04:44,084
May we enter!

37
00:04:47,084 --> 00:04:49,084
Pardon us, but it's time!

38
00:04:49,084 --> 00:04:52,084
We're going to need you to follow us down to the harbor right away!

39
00:04:52,084 --> 00:04:56,084
Without First Son of the Sea Jinbei, who is with Luffy,

40
00:04:56,084 --> 00:04:59,084
and Marshal D. Teach, who has burst into Impel Down,

41
00:04:59,084 --> 00:05:02,084
five of the seven warlords are about to leave Marie Joie.

42
00:05:04,084 --> 00:05:06,084
Among them is the infamous Boa Hancock,

43
00:05:06,084 --> 00:05:09,084
waiting in silence after her stop at Impel Down.

44
00:05:09,084 --> 00:05:14,084
Four of these five individuals have had dealings with the Straw Hat Pirates in the past.

45
00:05:15,084 --> 00:05:18,084
White Bits nothing but a tired old geezer,

46
00:05:18,084 --> 00:05:19,084
and look at the lot of you.

47
00:05:19,084 --> 00:05:21,084
Beside yourselves with fear.

48
00:05:21,084 --> 00:05:22,084
What's the big rush?

49
00:05:22,084 --> 00:05:25,084
We still have three hours before the execution.

50
00:05:26,084 --> 00:05:30,084
That's true, but I'm afraid we have to be prepared for any contingency, sir.

51
00:05:30,084 --> 00:05:31,084
That's true.

52
00:05:31,084 --> 00:05:32,084
That's true.

53
00:05:32,084 --> 00:05:33,084
That's true.

54
00:05:33,084 --> 00:05:34,084
That's true.

55
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:35,084
That's true.

56
00:05:35,084 --> 00:05:37,084
Now suffer the Ursa shock.

57
00:05:37,084 --> 00:05:49,084
I see you survived, Roro Noah.

58
00:05:49,084 --> 00:06:06,084
If you could take a vacation, where is it you'd like to go?

59
00:06:06,084 --> 00:06:11,084
I'll protect you, even if it costs me my life!

60
00:06:11,084 --> 00:06:15,084
Damn you!

61
00:06:15,084 --> 00:06:21,084
Someone help me!

62
00:06:21,084 --> 00:06:22,084
Robin!

63
00:06:22,084 --> 00:06:23,084
Loofy!

64
00:06:23,084 --> 00:06:40,084
You and I will never meet again.

65
00:06:40,084 --> 00:06:42,084
You and I will never meet again.

66
00:06:51,084 --> 00:06:52,084
Farewell, Striad.

67
00:06:52,084 --> 00:07:04,084
Can't wait to get your hands dirty, huh?

68
00:07:08,084 --> 00:07:10,084
Creepy as usual, I see.

69
00:07:11,084 --> 00:07:15,084
Dracule Mihawk, AKA Hawkeye Mihawk.

70
00:07:22,084 --> 00:07:46,084
That's...

71
00:07:48,084 --> 00:07:49,084
That's him.

72
00:07:49,084 --> 00:07:52,084
That man is...

73
00:07:52,084 --> 00:07:54,084
Hawkeye Mihawk.

74
00:07:57,084 --> 00:07:59,084
I set sail for only one reason.

75
00:07:59,084 --> 00:08:00,084
To meet you.

76
00:08:01,084 --> 00:08:03,084
And what is your goal?

77
00:08:03,084 --> 00:08:04,084
To beat you.

78
00:08:05,084 --> 00:08:06,084
How foolish.

79
00:08:10,084 --> 00:08:11,084
Tiger!

80
00:08:11,084 --> 00:08:12,084
Trap!

81
00:08:12,084 --> 00:08:19,084
Sir, state your name.

82
00:08:24,084 --> 00:08:26,084
I am Roan-O-Zoro.

83
00:08:27,084 --> 00:08:28,084
I'll remember it.

84
00:08:28,084 --> 00:08:31,084
No one as strong as you has come around in quite some time.

85
00:08:33,084 --> 00:08:38,084
So as a swordsman's courtesy, I'll use the world's strongest black sword to finish you.

86
00:08:38,084 --> 00:08:40,084
Three sword style secret technique!

87
00:08:43,084 --> 00:08:44,084
Five!

88
00:08:44,084 --> 00:08:45,084
Three thousand words!

89
00:09:00,084 --> 00:09:01,084
But why?

90
00:09:01,084 --> 00:09:04,084
Scars on the back are a swordsman's shame.

91
00:09:05,084 --> 00:09:06,084
Fine.

92
00:09:09,084 --> 00:09:10,084
SORROOOOO!

93
00:09:10,084 --> 00:09:20,084
You shouldn't rush these things, young man.

94
00:09:21,084 --> 00:09:23,084
There's nothing to be upset about.

95
00:09:23,084 --> 00:09:24,084
Your friend will live.

96
00:09:24,084 --> 00:09:27,084
It's still far too early for you to die.

97
00:09:28,084 --> 00:09:30,084
My name is Hawkeye Mihawk.

98
00:09:31,084 --> 00:09:33,084
You're strong, but there is much for you to learn.

99
00:09:34,084 --> 00:09:39,084
No matter how many years it takes, I will hold this title as the greatest in the world and wait for you.

100
00:09:40,084 --> 00:09:42,084
Until that day, you must hone your skills.

101
00:09:42,084 --> 00:09:46,084
Then, seek me out, Ro-Ro-Noah-Zoro!

102
00:09:51,084 --> 00:09:52,084
All right, I'm coming.

103
00:09:52,084 --> 00:09:54,084
Don't suppose I'd want to miss this.

104
00:09:55,084 --> 00:09:59,084
Might be a good chance to steal some more powerful shadows and corpses, after all.

105
00:10:00,084 --> 00:10:05,084
If any of Ace's little buddies try anything, it'll be an all-you-can-eat buffet for me.

106
00:10:05,084 --> 00:10:10,084
Gecko Maria

107
00:10:15,084 --> 00:10:21,084
Now, every last shadow in Thriller Bark come to me and become my power.

108
00:10:22,084 --> 00:10:25,084
Shadows has gone!

109
00:10:25,084 --> 00:10:46,084
GeckoBoy

110
00:10:47,084 --> 00:10:48,084
We will all fight!

111
00:10:49,084 --> 00:10:50,084
Grunt!

112
00:10:51,084 --> 00:10:53,084
We will turn to our fight.

113
00:10:53,084 --> 00:11:00,484
I call that one the black box!

114
00:11:00,484 --> 00:11:01,604
Dammit, you dropped me!

115
00:11:01,604 --> 00:11:02,924
I'll crush you!

116
00:11:16,884 --> 00:11:19,684
Consider this your punishment!

117
00:11:23,084 --> 00:11:32,404
Sorry, but Mr. Doflamingo and Ms. Hancock, you must hurry!

118
00:11:32,404 --> 00:11:33,924
Or what, little man?

119
00:11:33,924 --> 00:11:37,244
Who are you to give me orders?

120
00:11:37,244 --> 00:11:41,844
Or Hancock.

121
00:11:41,844 --> 00:11:48,964
The guilty thoughts swimming in your hearts shall turn your flesh to stone.

122
00:11:48,964 --> 00:11:53,284
Love, love, beam.

123
00:11:53,284 --> 00:11:58,284
I got it!

124
00:11:58,284 --> 00:12:00,284
Peace!

125
00:12:08,604 --> 00:12:10,604
Actually, you make me sick!

126
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:12,604
Stay strong, sister!

127
00:12:12,604 --> 00:12:14,604
This simply cannot be happening!

128
00:12:14,604 --> 00:12:17,604
There's no man alive that can resist my allure, it's just not possible!

129
00:12:17,604 --> 00:12:29,924
So long as that man exists in this world, I shall never know peace again!

130
00:12:29,924 --> 00:12:31,924
Medusa here!

131
00:12:31,924 --> 00:12:34,924
Eight-headed serpent!

132
00:12:34,924 --> 00:12:36,924
Medusa here!

133
00:12:36,924 --> 00:12:38,924
Salamander!

134
00:12:38,924 --> 00:12:42,204
Now come, go!

135
00:12:42,204 --> 00:12:44,244
And...

136
00:12:44,244 --> 00:12:48,244
badly!

137
00:12:48,244 --> 00:12:59,244
He can't be.

138
00:12:59,244 --> 00:13:03,244
You'd rather die than let people see this thing on your back, right?

139
00:13:03,244 --> 00:13:16,564
Like I said, don't move.

140
00:13:16,564 --> 00:13:21,004
Luffy, please be safe.

141
00:13:21,004 --> 00:13:29,964
This is the only one of the seven warlords of the sea who has never met Luffy or his crew.

142
00:13:29,964 --> 00:13:32,444
Don Quixote do Flamingo.

143
00:13:37,484 --> 00:13:38,764
No more!

144
00:13:38,764 --> 00:13:40,684
I'm begging you!

145
00:13:40,684 --> 00:13:42,524
Why are you making me do this?

146
00:13:42,524 --> 00:13:47,564
You've really let me down, and I've got zero tolerance for useless punks like you.

147
00:13:47,564 --> 00:13:48,924
No, not again!

148
00:13:48,924 --> 00:13:52,364
My body's moving on its own!

149
00:13:52,364 --> 00:13:54,364
I can't control it!

150
00:13:54,364 --> 00:13:55,244
Please!

151
00:13:55,244 --> 00:13:56,524
No!

152
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:04,684
Please...

153
00:14:04,684 --> 00:14:08,044
Just give me one more chance to set things right.

154
00:14:08,044 --> 00:14:11,244
I swear we'll loyally follow your every command.

155
00:14:13,804 --> 00:14:15,644
What a touching sentiment.

156
00:14:15,644 --> 00:14:17,244
Such genuine loyalty.

157
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:19,724
But...

158
00:14:19,724 --> 00:14:21,404
I still have no use for you.

159
00:14:24,444 --> 00:14:27,564
Doflamingo!

160
00:14:27,564 --> 00:14:32,524
The beginning is upon us.

161
00:14:33,084 --> 00:14:34,604
I suggest you prepare.

162
00:14:34,604 --> 00:14:38,684
We're drawing close to a new world in which only true pirates can survive.

163
00:14:39,324 --> 00:14:43,724
The weak should run while they still can, or be swept away by the tides of time,

164
00:14:43,724 --> 00:14:46,684
as they roll back to reveal a new era of champions.

165
00:14:46,684 --> 00:15:03,244
The extent of his strength is yet unknown.

166
00:15:03,244 --> 00:15:06,124
The end.

167
00:15:12,284 --> 00:15:15,964
There is another figure of interest at Navy headquarters.

168
00:15:16,764 --> 00:15:20,044
One who's under the command of Fleet Admiral Sengoku.

169
00:15:22,124 --> 00:15:25,964
Sorry to wake you, but we really need to get moving, Admiral.

170
00:15:25,964 --> 00:15:30,964
I'm up. It's already time for lunch, is it?

171
00:15:31,964 --> 00:15:33,964
Admiral Aokiji.

172
00:15:37,964 --> 00:15:39,964
Ice Age.

173
00:15:39,964 --> 00:15:57,964
The sea. It's... frozen.

174
00:15:58,964 --> 00:16:02,964
This is the power of a Navy Headquarters Admiral.

175
00:16:03,964 --> 00:16:08,964
You have some very loyal friends, but you will never change, Nico Robin.

176
00:16:08,964 --> 00:16:10,964
No. That's not true.

177
00:16:12,964 --> 00:16:15,964
Robin! Get away from him! Watch out!

178
00:16:29,964 --> 00:16:31,964
You bastard!

179
00:16:31,964 --> 00:16:37,964
Stop yelling. If you thaw her out carefully, she'll live.

180
00:16:38,964 --> 00:16:42,964
However, her body is extremely fragile, so you'll need to handle her with care.

181
00:16:43,964 --> 00:16:45,964
If she breaks, she'll die.

182
00:16:45,964 --> 00:16:48,964
For example, if I were to smash her apart...

183
00:16:48,964 --> 00:16:58,964
That was close.

184
00:16:59,964 --> 00:17:12,964
What in the hell are you doing?

185
00:17:13,964 --> 00:17:17,964
Usopp! Chop her! Quick! Take Robin and run back to the ship! Thaw her out and keep her safe!

186
00:17:17,964 --> 00:17:19,964
You're right! You got it, Captain!

187
00:17:19,964 --> 00:17:21,964
You're not glassed with this crew!

188
00:17:21,964 --> 00:17:23,964
Wait! Nobody attack him!

189
00:17:26,964 --> 00:17:30,964
Stay back and don't interfere. I'm gonna fight him one-on-one.

190
00:17:30,964 --> 00:17:37,964
What do you say? The two of us can settle this on our own!

191
00:17:38,964 --> 00:17:44,964
Fine by me. But since I don't have a ship to take you back, then I'll just have to kill you.

192
00:17:44,964 --> 00:17:45,964
I'll just have to kill you.

193
00:17:45,964 --> 00:17:46,964
I'll just have to kill you.

194
00:17:46,964 --> 00:17:48,964
I'll just have to kill you.

195
00:17:48,964 --> 00:18:01,964
Pockwongstar!

196
00:18:07,964 --> 00:18:14,964
Pockwongstar!

197
00:18:18,964 --> 00:18:27,724
Now, it's ice time.

198
00:18:42,044 --> 00:18:43,924
No, it's not lunch yet, Admiral.

199
00:18:44,124 --> 00:18:47,524
What I'm talking about is Portgus D. Ace's execution.

200
00:18:47,524 --> 00:18:52,124
I know that, kid. I was joking. Don't be so uptight.

201
00:18:54,644 --> 00:18:55,764
Please hurry, sir.

202
00:18:56,724 --> 00:18:58,804
Oh, they're summoning us at noon, huh?

203
00:18:59,044 --> 00:19:01,604
They could have at least let us eat our lunch first.

204
00:19:03,884 --> 00:19:05,284
Unruled Kizaru.

205
00:19:10,604 --> 00:19:11,004
Zoro!

206
00:19:12,684 --> 00:19:13,244
Ah!

207
00:19:17,524 --> 00:19:24,724
Who? Who are you? Uh, what are you?

208
00:19:24,924 --> 00:19:27,364
Whatever. Just get the hell away from Zoro!

209
00:19:27,884 --> 00:19:29,084
Oh, no, no. Zoro!

210
00:19:29,844 --> 00:19:32,084
He got hit by one of those laser beams!

211
00:19:32,924 --> 00:19:33,484
Kizaru?

212
00:19:33,704 --> 00:19:35,144
Hey, Usopp! Be careful!

213
00:19:35,604 --> 00:19:36,864
That man's a Navy Admiral!

214
00:19:36,864 --> 00:19:38,504
An admiral!

215
00:19:38,504 --> 00:19:40,024
Uh-oh!

216
00:19:40,984 --> 00:19:44,224
Well, you'll have plenty of time to rest up now.

217
00:19:46,824 --> 00:19:47,424
Zoro!

218
00:19:52,104 --> 00:19:53,984
Crap! He shoots beams, too?

219
00:19:54,184 --> 00:19:56,184
How are we supposed to beat these guys?

220
00:19:56,704 --> 00:19:58,884
At point blank like that, he's done for!

221
00:19:58,884 --> 00:20:02,484
Zoro's in trouble! Come on, do something, guys!

222
00:20:02,684 --> 00:20:04,684
Get away from him! Back up or else!

223
00:20:05,244 --> 00:20:05,724
Take this!

224
00:20:08,124 --> 00:20:09,764
What the hell? Why?

225
00:20:10,104 --> 00:20:11,984
What is this? What's happening?

226
00:20:12,324 --> 00:20:13,164
I can't hit him!

227
00:20:17,164 --> 00:20:19,004
I... I can't stab him!

228
00:20:19,224 --> 00:20:20,564
What the... What can we do?

229
00:20:20,564 --> 00:20:22,384
Trying? Damn it!

230
00:20:22,624 --> 00:20:24,344
Get back! Move your butt!

231
00:20:24,704 --> 00:20:25,384
I mean it!

232
00:20:25,704 --> 00:20:26,804
Leave him alone!

233
00:20:27,984 --> 00:20:29,964
Step away from our friend!

234
00:20:30,484 --> 00:20:31,944
You're wasting your time.

235
00:20:32,864 --> 00:20:34,164
I ate the Glinkland fruit,

236
00:20:34,244 --> 00:20:35,544
and now I'm made of light.

237
00:20:36,004 --> 00:20:37,524
It's a Logia, you see.

238
00:20:38,244 --> 00:20:39,424
He's made of light?

239
00:20:39,824 --> 00:20:40,984
This is a nightmare.

240
00:20:41,284 --> 00:20:42,424
There's nothing we can do.

241
00:20:42,784 --> 00:20:44,804
Zoro! Try to run away!

242
00:20:45,604 --> 00:20:46,884
Now, Van Taflu!

243
00:20:49,204 --> 00:20:49,804
Huh?

244
00:20:50,564 --> 00:20:58,504
It's cute how your friends want to save you,

245
00:20:58,784 --> 00:21:01,264
but you're far beyond help now.

246
00:21:04,164 --> 00:21:05,224
Well then,

247
00:21:05,924 --> 00:21:07,584
time to die.

248
00:21:07,584 --> 00:21:20,584
You picked some time to come out of hiding.

249
00:21:20,584 --> 00:21:24,544
You picked some time to come out of hiding.

250
00:21:24,544 --> 00:21:42,164
You sure you want to do this, Dark King Rayleigh?

251
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:43,624
Rayleigh!

252
00:21:43,624 --> 00:21:47,064
Don't go picking these buds before they sprout.

253
00:21:47,704 --> 00:21:49,624
Their era is only just beginning,

254
00:21:50,004 --> 00:21:51,664
and I want to see what they do with it.

255
00:21:54,564 --> 00:21:57,564
I suppose if Old Whitebeard is on the move,

256
00:21:57,684 --> 00:22:00,364
we must put duty ahead of our appetites, huh?

257
00:22:00,364 --> 00:22:06,904
Also at HQ is the Navy's extreme emissary of justice,

258
00:22:07,764 --> 00:22:09,144
Admiral Aka'inu.

259
00:22:09,144 --> 00:22:18,584
The Navy's greatest warriors,

260
00:22:19,584 --> 00:22:21,124
the three admirals,

261
00:22:22,044 --> 00:22:24,504
and the seven warlords of the sea.

262
00:22:27,004 --> 00:22:28,084
Gathered at Marineford,

263
00:22:28,084 --> 00:22:32,004
this formidable force stands between Luffy and his brother Ace.

264
00:22:32,004 --> 00:22:38,244
It's three hours to the execution.

265
00:22:38,664 --> 00:22:40,404
We have to take the prisoner to the scaffold.

266
00:22:48,644 --> 00:22:49,804
Time to go.

267
00:22:49,804 --> 00:23:12,664
50 warships, 100,000 marines,

268
00:23:12,664 --> 00:23:13,844
seven warlords,

269
00:23:14,164 --> 00:23:15,364
and the three Navy admirals,

270
00:23:15,524 --> 00:23:17,484
Aka'inu, Aokiji, and Kizaru.

271
00:23:17,484 --> 00:23:18,704
The stage is set,

272
00:23:18,944 --> 00:23:22,024
and Fleet Admiral Sengoku reveals a shocking truth

273
00:23:22,024 --> 00:23:24,624
as a battle with Whitebeard moves.

274
00:23:24,984 --> 00:23:25,604
On the next,

275
00:23:25,804 --> 00:23:26,364
One Piece,

276
00:23:26,644 --> 00:23:28,324
ticking down to the time of battle,

277
00:23:28,644 --> 00:23:30,944
the Navy's strongest lineup in position.

278
00:23:31,484 --> 00:23:33,304
Aikuku, King of the Pirates!

